      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Detect Ollama WorkOS sign-in redirects",
        "body": "## Summary\n- detect Ollama `/signin` redirects before attempting usage parsing\n- recognize the WorkOS AuthKit authorization destination on any `*.workos.com` host carrying the authorize path\n- surface expired-session recovery instead of a misleading parser failure\n\n## Proof\n\nDeterministic test run on this branch (injected HTTP transport — no network, no credentials):\n\n```text\n$ swift test --disable-sandbox --filter OllamaUsageFetcherTests\n◇ Test \"recognizes current ollama sign in redirects\" started.\n✔ Test \"recognizes current ollama sign in redirects\" passed\n✔ Test run with 19 tests in 1 suite passed.\n```\n\nWhen `ollama.com/settings` redirects to `/signin` or to a WorkOS `/user_management/authorize` page, the fetcher throws `invalidCredentials` instead of falling through to a parse failure, so CodexBar can try the next cookie candidate and show sign-in guidance.\n\n## Note for the maintainer\n\nThe exact redirect host Ollama's live session-expiry flow lands on is not network-verified here (no live account available). WorkOS AuthKit's canonical hosted authorize host is `auth.workos.com` (the server API host is `api.workos.com`), so the matcher accepts any `*.workos.com` host plus `ollama.com/signin` — intentionally broad to survive host changes/CNAMEs. This mirrors the in-repo Amp fetcher's broader `isLoginRedirect` heuristic.\n\n## Testing\n- `swift test --disable-sandbox --filter OllamaUsageFetcherTests` (19 passed, covering `auth.workos.com`, `api.workos.com`, and a non-WorkOS negative case)\n- `swift build` clean\n",
        "branch": "fix/ollama-reset-attribute-quotes",
